## Task

Compile a structured extraction report as JSON with this schema:

```json
{
  "pipeline_verdict": "pass | fail | partial",
  "overall_quality_score": <number from aggregate>,
  "materials_extracted": <total source documents processed>,
  "total_chunks": <chunk count>,
  "tagged_chunks": <tagged chunk count>,
  "embeddings_generated": <embedded chunk count>,
  "h_mems_stored": <assertion h_mem count>,
  "per_phase_summary": {
    "convert": {"quality_score": <number>, "verdict": "pass|fail"},
    "chunk": {"quality_score": <number>, "verdict": "pass|fail"},
    "tag": {"quality_score": <number>, "verdict": "pass|fail"},
    "embed": {"quality_score": <number>, "verdict": "pass|fail"},
    "extract_assertions": {"quality_score": <number>, "verdict": "pass|fail"}
  },
  "phases_at_iteration_ceiling": [<list of phase names that hit max iterations>],
  "corpus_query_verification": {
    "total_indexed": <number from verify_result>,
    "results_returned": <number of results from verify_result>,
    "verification_passed": <true if results_returned > 0>
  },
  "lessons_learned": [
    "<one-sentence lesson about what worked or failed>"
  ],
  "recommended_next_steps": [
    "<actionable next step for improving the corpus>"
  ]
}
```

The pipeline_verdict is "pass" if overall_quality_score >= 80, "partial" if
>= 50, and "fail" otherwise. Extract the per-phase scores from the aggregate
object. Count phases that may have hit the iteration ceiling by checking if
any Act steps produced non-empty adjustments.
